(Retirement communities were eligible if they were willing to present this study to their) Tj T*
(residents and provide space in their community to hold intervention sessions. We) Tj T*
(recruited communities through personal networks and professional organizations to ensure) Tj T*
(a diverse sample of communities based on rental rates/socioeconomic status,) Tj T*
(race/ethnicity of residents, and geographic area \(urban/suburban\). Participants with) Tj T*
(pre-frailty or frailty as determined by the SHARE-FI were enrolled in the study.) Tj T*
(Participants were >60 years of age, able to ambulate greater than 10 feet with moderate) Tj T*
(physical assistance or less with or without an assistive device and permanent residents) Tj T*
(of one of the enrolled independent living communities. Participants were excluded if) Tj T*
(they had uncontrolled cardiovascular, metabolic, renal, or respiratory disease that) Tj T*
(limited exercise participation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Recruitment, screening, and baseline testing) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Recruitment occurred via flyers and presentations at the enrolled retirement) Tj T*
(communities. Potential participants were screened using the Exercise Assessment and) Tj T*
(Screening for You [11] to determine if physician clearance for participation was needed.) Tj T*
(Participants who met inclusion criteria underwent baseline assessments administered by a) Tj T*
(licensed physical therapist. All assessments occurred on site at the retirement) Tj T*
(community utilizing standardized equipment to ensure consistency between sites.) Tj T*
(Recruitment began November 1st 2018, was paused due to the COVID-19 pandemic from March) Tj T*
(2020 to April 2021 and concluded in July 30th 2022.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Randomization and masking) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We randomized 14 independent living retirement communities to either a: 1\) high) Tj T*
(intensity \(HIW\) or 2\) casual speed \(CSW\) walking intervention. Retirement communities) Tj T*
(were randomized via a modified minimal sufficient balance randomization scheme for site) Tj T*
(level randomization by the unblinded statistical team \(S2 Table in S3 File\) [12]. Both) Tj T*
(the outcomes assessor and participants were blinded to group assignment. Since) Tj T*
(randomization occurred at the site level, participants were unaware of the other) Tj T*
(treatment arm as the consent materials indicated enrollment in a walking intervention) Tj T*
(with no mention of different walking intensities.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Intervention) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(All participants were scheduled for three sessions per week for the 16-week intervention) Tj T*
(which was delivered via one-on-one sessions led by a research assistant. All research) Tj T*
(assistants received approximately two weeks of training by the study PI in monitoring) Tj T*
(vitals and guarding participants during ambulation. All intervention sessions occurred) Tj T*
(within the hallways and stairwells at the participantís retirement community. The) Tj T*
(intervention consisted of three phases: Phase 1 ñ acclimation \(Week 1, sessions 1ñ3\),) Tj T*
(Phase 2 ñ ramp-up \(Weeks 2ñ4, sessions 4ñ12\), and Phase 3 ñ intervention \(Weeks 5ñ16,) Tj T*
(sessions 13ñ48\). The intention of a ramp up was to provide orientation to exercise prior) Tj T*
(to beginning the three-month intervention which was chosen as a minimum amount of time) Tj T*
(to see treatment effects. Details of each phase and walking activities are found in S3) Tj T*
(Table and S2 Table in S3 File. HIW participants aimed to achieve >70% of heart rate) Tj T*
(maximum \(HRmax\) or >15 on the Rating of Perceived Exertion \(RPE\) to facilitate high) Tj T*
(intensity while CSW participants walked at < 50% of HRmax or < 13 RPE. Given the impact) Tj T*
(of beta-blocker medications on heart rate and the high prevalence of beta-blocker use in) Tj T*
(our sample \(72%\), we used both HR and RPE to measure intensity [13].) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Prior to beginning the intervention, we estimated participantís HRmax using the Tanaka) Tj T*
(formula: Age-predicted HRmax?=?208ñ0.7 x age [14] and used the Karvonen formula [15].) Tj T*
([Target HR = \(HRmax-HRrest\) x %intensity\) + HRrest] to calculate each participantís) Tj T*
(target HR thresholds for 70% or 50% of HRmax depending on group assignment. Research) Tj T*
(assistants monitored heart rate throughout sessions using a Nonin pulse oximeter and) Tj T*
