(Physical Activity.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We used activPAL activity monitors placed on the thigh and worn for a one-week) Tj T*
(ambulatory monitoring period in the week preceding intervention start and immediately) Tj T*
(following intervention conclusion. The activPAL is a small, lightweight triaxial) Tj T*
(accelerometer that samples data at 20 Hz to record both durations and frequencies of) Tj T*
(walking, standing, sitting, and lying events. Data were processed using PAL Batch) Tj T*
(Software Suite version 7 [21]. We analyzed activPAL accelerometer data for those with at) Tj T*
(least 4 days of valid wear days for both baseline and follow-up to calculate reliable) Tj T*
(person-level estimates at each measurement occasion. A valid day was defined as a day) Tj T*
(with at least 10 waking hours of wear time [22]. We calculated average daily step count) Tj T*
(\(on valid days\) to represent physical activity volume.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Additional outcomes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We calculated each participantís average percentage of maximum heart rate across tasks) Tj T*
(excluding warm-up and cool-down \(measured heart rate divided by estimated maximum heart) Tj T*
(rate for each task and then averaged across the seven tasks in each session\) to) Tj T*
(calculate average exercise intensity. Adherence was determined by the number the) Tj T*
(exercise sessions completed out of a possible 48 sessions. The study developed) Tj T*
(guidelines for adherence which defined a completed session as one in which a participant) Tj T*
(completed at least four out of seven walking tasks. Participants who completed more than) Tj T*
(50% of tasks \(4/7\) tasks per session for at least 80% of Phase 3 intervention sessions) Tj T*
(\(29/36 sessions\) were considered to have ìcompletedî the 16-week intervention and were) Tj T*
(considered in the per-protocol analysis. Adverse events were monitored during each) Tj T*
(intervention session and as reported by participants throughout the 16-week) Tj T*
(intervention.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Statistical analysis) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Descriptive statistics were used to summarize participant characteristics, as well as) Tj T*
(session-level data to characterize adherence to the protocol and dose of the) Tj T*
(intervention as indicators of treatment fidelity. The RPE and HR values were averaged) Tj T*
(across all tasks within a session \(excluding the warm-up and cool-down\) for each) Tj T*
(participant and then averaged across all intervention phase sessions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Analyses were based on a modified intention-to-treat \(ITT\) principle, whereby all) Tj T*
(randomized participants with post-intervention data on at least one outcome measure were) Tj T*
(included in the analysis, regardless of number of completed sessions. Data from two) Tj T*
(participants from the CSW arm and one in the HIW arm did not have follow-up SHARE-FI) Tj T*
(data due to REDCap data loss which is why n?=?102 were analyzed. Sensitivity analyses) Tj T*
(were conducted using the per-protocol sample.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The primary analysis used a generalized linear mixed model to estimate the odds of) Tj T*
(improvement in frailty category at 16 weeks in the HIW arm compared to the CSW arm. The) Tj T*
(model included fixed effects for arm and baseline SHARE-FI score. A random site effect) Tj T*
(accounted for clustering of participants within a retirement center. Linear mixed models) Tj T*
(were employed for secondary outcomes with fixed arm and baseline scores, and a random) Tj T*
(cluster effect. A similar model with random participant effect was used to compare) Tj T*
(changes in physical activity data over time. A pre-specified gatekeeping approach) Tj T*
(controlled for multiple testing of primary and secondary outcome families. Specifically,) Tj T*
(the primary outcome was tested at a 5% level of significance, and the secondary outcome) Tj T*
(family was tested at an overall 5% level of significance only following a significant) Tj T*
(primary outcome. The Hochberg approach was employed within the secondary outcome family) Tj T*
(to account for multiple testing. Sensitivity analyses also considered imputations for) Tj T*
(missing data.) Tj T*
