(threshold for clinical meaningful change in frailty index scores [26,27]. The) Tj T*
(combination of aerobic and resistive aerobic activities in our approach may have) Tj T*
(provided sufficient neuromuscular stimulus by increasing frequency and intensity of) Tj T*
(activity, despite a shorter intervention duration, to drive improvements in frailty) Tj T*
(category. Our study advances evidence for the optimal dose of therapeutic interventions) Tj T*
(for the frailty and provides clear evidence on the substantial benefits of high-) Tj T*
(intensity walking to decrease and reverse frailty among those with existing frailty. Our) Tj T*
(approach, which incorporated some resistance elements into aerobic training, was) Tj T*
(distinct.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Mobility) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In addition to reducing frailty, HIW improved gait speed and 6-minute walk distance.) Tj T*
(Previous work in both healthy older adults and those with neurologic impairment shows) Tj T*
(greater amounts of walking practice at higher intensities is associated with superior) Tj T*
(gains in walking performance [28]. Both treatment groups in our study increased walking) Tj T*
(volume, but HIW participants achieved greater mobility gains suggesting intensity may be) Tj T*
(the critical parameter to facilitate mobility improvements. Both treatment groups) Tj T*
(improved fast gait speed and SPPB in excess of 50% above the MCID threshold with the HIW) Tj T*
(group having a larger change from baseline in both measures.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Physical activity volume) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Beyond mobility improvements, HIW produced substantial improvements in daily physical) Tj T*
(activity \(PA\) compared to CSW. Evidence on whether PA programs can modify daily walking) Tj T*
(behavior is mixed. Some studies report people compensate for exercise participation by) Tj T*
(reducing ambulatory PA [29]. while others find no change in ambulatory PA after) Tj T*
(participating in structured exercise. According to the COM-B model of behavior change) Tj T*
([30]. physical capacity is a key determinant of activity behavior. Prior research finds) Tj T*
(low physical capability restricts participation in daily life events among frail older) Tj T*
(adults. Further, older adults with frailty average three minutes per week in moderate-) Tj T*
(vigorous physical activity, 85% of waking hours are spent in sedentary behavior \(i.e.,) Tj T*
(sitting\), and average daily walking is less than 2,000 steps per day [31]. Thus,) Tj T*
(improving capability may contribute to improved PA participation and greater amounts of) Tj T*
(daily walking. We found HIW participants increased PA volume by 496 steps per day from) Tj T*
(baseline. Wright et. al., reported that the median effect of physical activity) Tj T*
(interventions on older adults was estimated to be 398 steps/day [32]. Our 985-step) Tj T*
(between group difference places this effect over the 95th percentile based on seven) Tj T*
(meta-analyses of 160 trials with over 73,000 older adults [33]. These findings suggest) Tj T*
(HIW meaningfully improves capability and transfers into greater daily activity which is) Tj T*
(one of the first findings of the benefits of HIW transfer to post-intervention) Tj T*
(ambulatory PA.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Physical function) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(HIW participants also improved their physical function. The change in SPPB score among) Tj T*
(HIW participants is higher than the change seen in both the REACT trial [33] and the) Tj T*
(LIFE study [34]. A chief difference between those studies and our approach is intensity) Tj T*
(of the intervention with low to moderate intensities in REACT and LIFE. Our finding) Tj T*
(suggests that older adults with frailty may require a more intense intervention to) Tj T*
(elicit functional improvements. As aging is associated with reductions in aerobic) Tj T*
(capacity, cardiac output, and other measures of cardiovascular health, lower intensity) Tj T*
(training may not provide a sufficient physiologic stimulus to induct meaningful) Tj T*
(cardiovascular or metabolic adaptions. In contrast, HIW likely produces greater) Tj T*
(cardiorespiratory demand, resulting in increased physiologic reserve and physical) Tj T*
(function.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
